  "provenance_boundary": "Published crate files are the provenance baseline, not a claim that normalized Cargo.toml is repository-identical. The platform adapter is new rd-engine integration, not code transplanted from the selected RustDesk pin.",
  "runtime_requirements": [
    "Use a synchronous FRB/account worker with the existing common private-store file lock held; do not call from an asynchronous executor thread.",
    "A reachable per-user session DBus and Secret Service implementing encrypted DH sessions and an already-unlocked persistent default collection are required; this adapter never manually starts/provisions a service, creates a collection, unlocks, or executes a prompt.",
    "The integration owner's selected policy allows ordinary D-Bus service activation by the maintained client. No NO_AUTO_START/unique-owner transport variation is added; upstream destination behavior remains unchanged.",
    "Secret Service does not standardize access control, persistent-collection classification, atomic compare-and-set uniqueness, or disk fsync. Deployment must provide a trustworthy persistent default collection and service security policy. Add-only creation is serialized for cooperative callers by the common file lock and conflicts are rejected by exact lookup/readback.",
    "The adapter zeroizes returned temporary secret bytes. The unmodified client/transport may retain cryptographic/session/serialization temporaries until normal deallocation; no guarantee of whole-process memory erasure is made."
  ],
